g independently rules it out: 1010's lone event falls in (57001,60000] while 883's two events fall in (62501,65000] and (70001,75000] (step_14/step_15) \u2014 gaps of thousands of time units, far exceeding the 600-unit relay limit. Confounders checked: the window is busy overall (6477 events, 1922 active nodes, step_01) and dominated by hubs such as 158/1726/639 (step_11) that are unrelated to this pair; both nodes are modestly active over all time (6 and 11 events, step_21) and sit on essentially no triangles (step_19), so global volume and popularity, not any genuine temporal pathway, are what create the appearance of a connection.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 75326, "total_output_tokens": 6361, "total_tokens": 81687, "total_latency_ms": 96073, "llm_calls": 12, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}